.TH PLUGIN-QUALIFY-RECORDS-PACKAGE 1 "October 2026" "plugin-qualify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-qualify-records-package \- the Debian packages of a device's qualification records, one per rate and quantum
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-qualify-records-package
.IR qualification-dir | run-root ...
[\fB\-\-cell\fR \fIrate\fB/\fIquantum\fR] \fB\-\-host\-class\fR \fIclass\fR \fB\-\-set\fR \fIset\fR \fB\-\-provenance\fR \fIjson\fR
[\fB\-\-version\fR \fIversion\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-maintainer\fR \fIwho\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A record set is per machine class, rate and quantum. Builds one
\fBplugin-db-qualification-\fIclass\fB-\fIset\fB-\fIrate\fB-\fIquantum\fB_\fIversion\fB_all.deb\fR per cell, a package of plugin-db's
qualification layer, from the qualification directories plugin-qualify-sync(1) left on a device: each directory is a
cell, named by its base (\fIrun\fB/b48000-512/qualification\fR), and a run root stands for every
\fBb\fIrate\fB-\fIquantum\fB/qualification\fR under it. Each package installs every record of its cell, with the probe
output it judged, under /usr/share/omx/qualification/\fIclass\fR/\fIset\fB-\fIrate\fB-\fIquantum\fR/ beside
\fBprovenance.json\fR, which names the cell, and depends on the minor
of the plugin-qualify that wrote it, up to the next minor. On another device of the class, plugin-qualify-sync takes a plugin from
those records instead of measuring it, and only when every file of the installed plugin hashes as the measured one
did.
.PP
A record whose probe output is missing, or is not the copy it names, is left out and named on standard error; so is
an unmeasured record, which never applies, and a record whose grid does not hold its set's cell. Each line on standard
output names one package, its set and cell, its records and its files. Two directories of one cell, or a directory
whose records hold several cells and whose name says none, are refused before any package is written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host\-class " class"
The machine class the records were measured on (\fBrpi5\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-set " set"
The plugin set they cover (\fBzynthian-vangelis\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-cell " rate/quantum"
The cell of one directory whose name says none and whose records hold several.
.TP
.BI \-\-provenance " json"
A JSON file, or the JSON itself, with what the tool cannot know: the image, the package versions and the source
revisions of the device. The set, the class, the package and the date are added.
.TP
.BI \-\-version " version"
The package's version; the default is the build date, \fB2026.10.29\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " dir"
Where the package is written (default: the current directory).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 every package was written; 2 one could not be.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plugin-qualify-sync (1)
